---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AiSummary from '../../components/AiSummary.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import Byline from '../../components/Byline.astro';
import { certifications } from '../../data/certifications';
import { careers } from '../../data/careers';
import { site, teamBySlug } from '../../data/site';
import { certRankingLinks } from '../../data/ranking-copy';
import { outcomesSurvey } from '../../data/research';
import bls from '../../data/bls.json';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return certifications.map(cert => ({ params: { slug: cert.slug }, props: { cert } }));
}

const { cert } = Astro.props;
const author = teamBySlug[cert.author] ?? site.team[0];
const occ = bls.occupations as Record<string, any>;
const rdn = bls.occupations['dietitians-nutritionists'];
const relatedCareers = careers
  .filter(c => c.certifications.includes(cert.slug))
  .map(c => ({ career: c, data: c.bls ? occ[c.bls] : null }));
const rankingLinks = certRankingLinks[cert.slug] ?? [];

const wordCount = [
  cert.takeaway, cert.hotTake, cert.for,
  ...cert.facts.map(f => f[1]),
  ...cert.costs.rows.map(r => r[1]),
  ...cert.studyResources,
  ...cert.sections.flatMap(s => [...s.paragraphs, ...(s.bullets ?? [])]),
  ...cert.faq.map(f => f.answer)
].join(' ').split(/\s+/).length;

const credentialSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'EducationalOccupationalCredential',
  name: cert.title,
  alternateName: cert.short,
  description: cert.takeaway,
  credentialCategory: 'certification',
  recognizedBy: { '@type': 'Organization', name: cert.issuer, url: cert.issuerUrl },
  url: new URL(`/certifications/${cert.slug}/`, site.url).toString()
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title={`${cert.title} (${cert.short}): Requirements, Exam, and Cost`}
  description={`${cert.short} credential guide: eligibility requirements, examination detail, real costs, study resources, and what it actually permits you to do. Issued by ${cert.issuer}.`}
  article={{ section: 'Certifications', author: author.name }}
>
  <script slot="head" is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(credentialSchema)} />

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">{cert.short}</p>
      <h1>{cert.title}</h1>
      <p class="lede">{cert.takeaway}</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" href={cert.issuerUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          {cert.issuer} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="content wrap">
    <Byline author={author} />

    <AiSummary>
      {cert.title}, abbreviated {cert.short}, is issued by {cert.issuer}. {cert.takeaway} Who it is for:
      {' '}{cert.for} Key requirements at a glance: {cert.facts.slice(0, 3).map(f => `${f[0]}, ${f[1]}`).join(' ')}
      {' '}Federal context: the Bureau of Labor Statistics reported a May 2024 median annual wage of
      {' '}${rdn.median.toLocaleString()} for dietitians and nutritionists against
      {' '}${bls.allOccupationsMedian.toLocaleString()} for all occupations, and our own {outcomesSurvey.shortName} of
      {' '}{outcomesSurvey.sampleLabel} found {outcomesSurvey.headline.employerHiringDifficulty} percent of employers
      struggling to find qualified RDN candidates. Fees, eligibility rules, and continuing education requirements are
      set by the issuing body and change, so confirm everything on this page directly with {cert.issuer} before you
      spend money. Reviewed by {author.name}, {author.role}. Last updated {site.reviewedLabel}.
    </AiSummary>

    <div class="hot-take">
      <strong>Our take</strong>
      <p>{cert.hotTake}</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Who this credential is for</h2>
    <p>{cert.for}</p>

    <h2>The requirements, line by line</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {cert.facts.map(([label, detail]) => (
            <tr><td><strong>{label}</strong></td><td>{detail}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Every line above should be confirmed with
      {' '}<a href={cert.issuerUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{cert.issuer}</a> before you act on it.
      Credentialing bodies revise requirements, and a page on a third-party site, including this one, is not the
      authority on what you owe them this year.
    </p>

    <h2>What it costs, honestly</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>{cert.costs.head[0]}</th><th>{cert.costs.head[1]}</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {cert.costs.rows.map(([label, detail]) => (
            <tr><td><strong>{label}</strong></td><td>{detail}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      We describe cost categories rather than quoting dollar figures for fees that change annually, because a stale
      number is worse than no number. The categories are the useful part: they tell you what to budget for, including
      the lines candidates routinely forget.
    </p>

    <h2>How to prepare</h2>
    <ul>{cert.studyResources.map(resource => <li>{resource}</li>)}</ul>

    <Prose sections={cert.sections} />

    {relatedCareers.length > 0 && (
      <>
        <h2>Careers this credential supports</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Career</th><th>Track</th><th>Federal median wage</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {relatedCareers.map(({ career, data }) => (
                <tr>
                  <td><a href={`/careers/${career.slug}/`}>{career.title}</a></td>
                  <td>{career.track}</td>
                  <td>{data ? `$${data.median.toLocaleString()}` : 'No separate federal code'}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>What this means for you</h2>
    <p>
      Before you commit money, do three things. Confirm the current eligibility rules with
      {' '}<a href={cert.issuerUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{cert.issuer}</a> directly. Read twenty
      live job postings for the roles you want and count how many name this credential specifically. And check your own
      state board, because a national credential and a state licence are different instruments and only one of them
      controls whether you may practise.
    </p>
    <p>
      If the postings do not name it and your state does not require it, the credential may still be worth holding, but
      you should be able to say out loud what you expect it to buy you. Credentials collected without a reason are an
      expensive hobby.
    </p>
    <p>
      Related reading:
      {rankingLinks.map(([href, label]) => (
        <>
          {' '}<a class="text-link" href={href}>{label}</a>,
        </>
      ))}
      {' '}<a class="text-link" href="/careers/">career guides by occupation</a>,
      {' '}<a class="text-link" href="/resources/how-to-become-a-registered-dietitian-step-by-step/">the step by step RDN pathway</a>, and
      {' '}<a class="text-link" href="/resources/nutrition-career-outcomes/">the Career Outcomes Survey 2026</a>.
    </p>

    <Faq items={cert.faq} />

    <div class="notice">
      <Byline author={author} prefix="Reviewed by" />
      <strong>Confirm at source:</strong> {cert.issuer} sets the requirements, fees, and continuing education rules for
      this credential and revises them periodically. Nothing on this page is a substitute for their published
      documentation, and nothing here is legal advice about scope of practice. State licensure is separate from
      certification and is governed by your state board. Last reviewed {site.reviewedLabel}. This guide runs roughly
      {' '}{wordCount.toLocaleString()} words.
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap }
</style>
